<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">A TTI conjecture &middot; the dark scaffold becoming luminous</p>
  <h1>JWST&rsquo;s Little Red Dots, Through TTI</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Suppose the little red dots are not a fourth kind of cosmic substance. Suppose they
    are a short-lived <em>transition</em>: compact places where the dark scaffold of partial integration is
    being forced across a seam into the luminous, complex phase of matter.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame frame--first illuminated">
    <p class="kicker">The speculation in one sentence</p>
    <h2 id="t-proposal">A Little Red Dot Is an Integration Front</h2>
    <p class="lede">In the language of The Shape of Becoming, a little red dot would be a young galactic
      nucleus caught while its local integration field climbs from the dark-matter-like middle state
      \(\chi\simeq\tfrac12\) toward luminous baryonic completion at \(\chi\simeq1\).</p>
    <p>The black hole at the centre supplies the most extreme closure boundary in the region. Matter and
      partially integrated geometry circulate around it, compress, heat and cross a narrow transition zone.
      Ordinary gas physics turns the escaping light red; TTI&rsquo;s additional claim is about <em>why this
      compact transitional arrangement should be common in the young universe</em>.</p>
    <p>The dot is therefore neither a miniature finished galaxy nor a permanent species. It is the glow of a
      seam while a dark gravitational scaffold becomes capable of carrying phase, electromagnetism and light.
      When the surrounding host completes and spreads that integration, the object ceases to satisfy the
      little-red-dot selection even though the black hole and galaxy remain. <span class="spec">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p class="muted small">Grading on this page: <span class="sci">&#9670; the minimal observational anchor</span>
      &middot; <span class="spec">&#9670; a conditional TTI mechanism</span> &middot;
      <span class="myth">&#9670; philosophical image only</span>. The mechanism below is a new extension of
      the framework, not an established result and not yet a solution of its own field equations.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The sky, kept brief</p>
    <h2 id="t-observation">What the Conjecture Is Trying to Explain</h2>
    <p>Webb has found an abundant early population of extremely compact sources with blue rest-ultraviolet
      light, steep red rest-optical continua and, in many examples, spectral evidence for accreting massive
      black holes. They become common in the first billion years and decline rapidly later. Dense gas around
      young black holes is presently the leading physical account of their unusual spectra.
      <span class="sci">&#9670;</span></p>
    <p>TTI does not replace that radiative-transfer account. It places a speculative geometric process beneath
      it: the cocoon is the material expression of an integration boundary, and the rapidly growing black hole
      is the centre around which the boundary closes. The observed redness still comes from atoms, gas,
      scattering, absorption and cosmological redshift. There is no special &ldquo;red frequency&rdquo; in the
      \(\chi\)-field.</p>
  </div>
</section>

